00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.777
You talked about
App Engine, which

00:10:29.777 --> 00:10:31.420
is an application as a service.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.470
You build an application,
we scale it for you.

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:35.470
But sometimes you don't
need a full application,

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.180
you just need a
little bit of code.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:40.420
One little bit of code
that will do one thing.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:44.200
Enter Cloud Functions, event
driven serverless functions.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.140
What you can do is have a
function, a single function,

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.500
respond to an event.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.830
And that event
could be HTTP-based,

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:54.638
so you get a URL that you
can use to hit your code.

00:10:54.638 --> 00:10:56.680
Or it could be something
what we call background.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.250
Background is writing
a file to a bucket

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:03.710
or responding to a
message on Pub/Sub.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.290
Languages, we have a restricted
set of languages here--

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:09.777
Node.js, Python and Go.

